# Copy to .env and fill in. Only .env.example is committed.

# ─── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ─── Multi-tenancy — which hotel this deployment serves ───────────────────────
# One deployment = one hotel. Both are the SAME slug from the `tenants` table;
# they exist separately because one is public (browser) and one is a boundary.
#
#   VITE_TENANT_SLUG — inlined into the bundle. Sent as the x-tenant-slug header
#     to scope PUBLIC anon reads (room types, rates, published reviews). A hint
#     only, spoofable by design — it can surface just another hotel's brochure.
#
#   TENANT_SLUG — server only, no VITE_ prefix. Authoritative: decides which
#     hotel a new profile is filed under at first SSO login. Never from client.
#
# Leave BOTH unset on a single-hotel install — the database falls back to the
# sole tenant and fails closed the moment a second hotel is added.
# VITE_TENANT_SLUG=gostay
# TENANT_SLUG=gostay

# ─── Ventera SSO — public (inlined into the browser bundle) ───────────────────
VITE_SSO_ISSUER=https://sso.ventera.ai
VITE_SSO_CLIENT_ID=gostay

# ─── Ventera SSO — server only ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No VITE_ prefix, so Vite never inlines these into client code. Read by the
# token exchange in api/sso/token.ts (and the matching Vite dev middleware).
# On Vercel, set them as Environment Variables — not here.
SSO_ISSUER=https://sso.ventera.ai
SSO_CLIENT_ID=gostay
SSO_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here
# Optional: extra origins allowed to run a token exchange, comma-separated.
# localhost and *.vercel.app are always allowed.
# SSO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://gostay.example.com

# Public base URL of the app (guest portal). The WhatsApp bot builds each hotel's
# portal link from it — `${APP_PUBLIC_URL}/portal?hotel={slug}`. Defaults to the
# production app domain when unset.
# APP_PUBLIC_URL=https://app.gostay.id

# Optional: the role a NEW profile is created with on first web sign-in. Defaults
# to 'customer' (least privilege, tenant-safe) — hotel staff are created via the
# onboarding wizard / self-serve tenant flow, not by a plain web signup (see role
# model in docs/PRD-GoStay-Hotel-System.md §2). It only stamps the initial row;
# profiles.role stays the source of truth afterwards.
# SSO_SIGNUP_ROLE=customer

# ─── Supabase identity bridge — server only ──────────────────────────────────
# Without these the browser talks to Supabase as anon, auth.uid() is NULL and
# every RLS policy denies. Sign-in still works; the app just reads public data.
#
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET: Supabase Dashboard > Settings > API > JWT Secret.
#   Used to sign the token that carries the SSO identity into Postgres.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: same page. Bypasses RLS — server only, never VITE_.
#   Used solely to create a user's profiles row on first login.
# SUPABASE_URL: defaults to VITE_SUPABASE_URL when unset.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=your-supabase-jwt-secret
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# profiles.id is uuid_v5(this namespace, sso_sub). CHANGING IT REMAPS EVERY
# USER and orphans their bookings, chats and audit rows. Leave unset.
# SSO_UUID_NAMESPACE=b9c1a7d4-3e52-4f68-9a0b-7d2c5e814f36

# ─── WhatsApp AI booking — server only ───────────────────────────────────────
# Read by the WA webhook (api/wa/*, api/_lib/wa/*), a Vercel Node function. No
# VITE_ prefix — none of these may ever reach the browser bundle. On Vercel, set
# them as Environment Variables, not here.
#
# SSO_VENTERA_PROVISION_URL + PROVISION_API_KEY: mint a guest an SSO account by
#   phone, no browser. The webhook POSTs {phone,displayName?} to
#   <SSO_VENTERA_PROVISION_URL>/api/admin/users/provision with
#   `Authorization: Bearer <PROVISION_API_KEY>`; Ventera returns { ok, sub }.
#   Same value as Ventera's own PROVISION_API_KEY. A boundary secret — leaking it
#   lets anyone mint accounts, so treat it like the service-role key.
# SSO_VENTERA_PROVISION_URL=https://sso.ventera.ai
# PROVISION_API_KEY=your-ventera-provision-key

# ─── WhatsApp gateway (wa-ventera) — inbound webhook, server only ────────────
# WA_WEBHOOK_SECRET: the shared secret wa-ventera sends in the `x-webhook-secret`
#   header when it POSTs inbound messages to <this app>/api/wa/inbound. The route
#   rejects any request whose header does not match (constant-time). Must equal
#   the `secret` in this hotel's WEBHOOK_ROUTES entry on the gateway. No VITE_
#   prefix. When unset, the webhook denies every caller (fails closed).
# WA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-inbound-webhook-secret
#
# ─── WhatsApp gateway (wa-ventera) — outbound send, server only ──────────────
# No VITE_ prefix, so Vite never inlines these into client code. Read by the
# outbound helper api/_lib/wa/send.ts to reply to a guest through the gateway.
# On Vercel, set them as Environment Variables — not here.
#
# WA_VENTERA_BASE_URL: base URL of the wa-ventera gateway. The helper POSTs to
#   <base>/api/sessions/<sessionId>/send. A trailing slash is trimmed.
# WA_VENTERA_INT_KEY: integration key (an `int_*` value) sent as
#   `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Its owner MUST be an owner/admin of the
#   target hotel session, or the gateway answers 401/403. NEVER commit a real
#   key and never give it a VITE_ prefix. When either var is unset the helper
#   returns { ok:false, error:"send_not_configured" } instead of sending.
# WA_VENTERA_BASE_URL=https://wa.ventera.ai
# WA_VENTERA_INT_KEY=int_your-integration-key-here

# ─── WhatsApp anti-spam — server only, all optional ──────────────────────────
# Every value below has a working default; set one only to tune or to test.
#
# WA_ALLOWED_GUESTS: comma-separated numbers that may be auto-answered. LEAVE
#   UNSET IN PRODUCTION — unset means "answer everyone", which is what a hotel
#   with its own dedicated WhatsApp number wants.
#
#   Set it only while a PERSONAL phone is linked as a hotel's WhatsApp for
#   testing. Without it, every contact who texts that phone is an ordinary
#   one-to-one chat containing a trigger word, so they receive the hotel's
#   reservation menu — spam sent to a real person. Digits are compared, so
#   +62, spaces and dashes are all fine.
# WA_ALLOWED_GUESTS=6281234567890,6289876543210
#
# WA_REPLY_MAX / WA_REPLY_WINDOW: per-number reply budget. Bounds a burst if a
#   backlog ever slips past the freshness guard. Default 8 per '1 minute'.
# WA_REPLY_MAX=8
# WA_REPLY_WINDOW=1 minute
#
# WA_GREET_COOLDOWN: how often ONE number may receive the built-in welcome.
#   Default '1 hour'.
# WA_GREET_COOLDOWN=1 hour
#
# WA_FLOW_START_MAX / WA_FLOW_START_WINDOW: how often the same hotel-authored
#   flow may be restarted for one number. Guards a third-party loop, which the
#   fromMe filter cannot see. Default 3 per '10 minutes'.
# WA_FLOW_START_MAX=3
# WA_FLOW_START_WINDOW=10 minutes
#
# WA_MAX_AUTO_REPLY_AGE_MS: messages older than this are treated as replayed
#   history and never auto-answered — the guard that stops a freshly-linked
#   session greeting an entire backlog. Default 300000 (5 minutes).
# WA_MAX_AUTO_REPLY_AGE_MS=300000
#
# WA_GREETING_TRIGGERS: overrides the built-in greeting openers (comma-separated).
# WA_GREETING_TRIGGERS=halo,hai,menu,info

# ─── AI chat provider — server only ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Every chat-completions caller — booking-intent extraction (api/_lib/wa/ai.ts),
# the guest concierge (api/_lib/wa/concierge.ts), and the outbound sales writer
# (api/_lib/outbound/*) — goes through api/_lib/ai/chat.ts. No VITE_ prefix on
# ANY key here: none of them may ever reach the browser bundle.
#
# AI_CHAT_PROVIDER: ordered failover chain, comma-separated. Tried left to
#   right; one that fails (out of credit, rate limited, down) hands over to the
#   next. A provider whose key is empty is skipped, so the key of an inactive
#   vendor can stay here and the chain flips back by editing one variable.
#     openai       → OpenAI only (the default when this is unset)
#     nous         → Nous Portal only
#     nous,openai  → Nous first, fall back to OpenAI
# AI_CHAT_PROVIDER=openai
#
# NOT covered: Voice AI (api/_lib/voice/handlers.ts) uses OpenAI's Realtime API,
# which has no equivalent elsewhere — it always needs OPENAI_API_KEY.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY: also the key Voice AI uses. With no usable provider, intent
#   extraction still works through a deterministic regex/keyword fallback (lower
#   confidence) and the concierge degrades to "let me get staff".
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL: defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_API_URL: overrides the chat-completions endpoint. Leave unset in
#   production (defaults to https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions); it
#   exists so tests can point extraction at a local mock server.
# OPENAI_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
#
# NOUS_API_KEY: Nous Portal (https://portal.nousresearch.com), an OpenAI-
#   compatible multi-vendor gateway.
# NOUS_API_KEY=sk-nous-...
# NOUS_CHAT_MODEL: defaults to nousresearch/hermes-4-70b — fast, cheap, and it
#   supports tool calling, which the concierge depends on entirely.
# NOUS_CHAT_MODEL=nousresearch/hermes-4-70b
# NOUS_API_URL: defaults to
#   https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1/chat/completions
# NOUS_API_URL=

# ─── Payments — via the central Ventera gateway (server only) ─────────────────
# GoStay does NOT hold Xendit keys. The Ventera gateway holds them (sandbox +
# live), creates invoices, and forwards Xendit settlement callbacks to GoStay's
# /api/payment/webhook. GoStay authenticates to/from the gateway with a per-
# environment internal token — the same `x-internal-token` scheme as Storo.
# None of these ever reach the browser — no VITE_ prefix. On Vercel set them as
# Environment Variables, not here.
#
# The per-hotel live/test toggle is set by the Ventera super admin in the app
# (Supabase + RLS), NOT here — this only picks which token authenticates.
#
# XENDIT_API_KEY_SANDBOX / _PRODUCTION: the Xendit secret keys GoStay uses to
#   CREATE invoices. Sandbox keys look like xnd_development_…, live like
#   xnd_production_…. Two variables rather than one key plus a mode flag, so a
#   hotel in test mode physically cannot reach the live key.
# XENDIT_API_KEY_SANDBOX=xnd_development_...
# XENDIT_API_KEY_PRODUCTION=xnd_production_...
#
# INTERNAL_TOKEN_PRODUCTION / _SANDBOX: the shared secrets the VENTERA GATEWAY
#   presents when it forwards a Xendit callback to /api/payment/webhook. They
#   authenticate the RETURN leg only — GoStay never sends them anywhere. Copy
#   them from the gateway's routing table (prefix GOSTAY), and paste the value
#   WITHOUT surrounding quotes: the check is a byte comparison, so a stray quote
#   rejects every callback with no obvious cause.
# INTERNAL_TOKEN_PRODUCTION=replace-with-the-gostay-live-internal-token
# INTERNAL_TOKEN_SANDBOX=replace-with-the-gostay-sandbox-internal-token
#
# There is deliberately no gateway URL: the gateway has no invoice endpoint, and
# Xendit's callback URL is configured once in the Xendit dashboard.

# ─── Granting the first admin (one-time) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Roles live in profiles.role, not in this file and not in the SSO. Everyone who
# signs in gets 'customer' by default, and only an admin may promote anyone
# ("Admin can update any profile" in 002_rls_policies.sql) — so the first admin
# has to be made once, by hand, or nobody can ever grant anyone anything.
#
# Sign in once so your profile row exists, then run this in the Supabase SQL
# editor (it runs as the table owner and bypasses RLS):
#
#   update profiles set role = 'admin' where email = 'you@ventera.ai';
#
# After that, promote and demote everyone else from User Management.

# ─── Outbound Lead Generation (GoStay Sales Bot) ─────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: used by api/outbound/wa/generate.ts and converse.ts to
#   generate personalized sales messages and handle lead conversations via Claude.
#   Required for the agentic lead gen system.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# WA_OUTBOUND_SESSION_ID: the wa-ventera session ID of the GoStay sales WA number.
#   Configure WEBHOOK_ROUTES[this-id] → /api/outbound/wa/inbound in wa-ventera.
# WA_OUTBOUND_SESSION_ID=gostay-sales

# WA_OUTBOUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET: separate secret from WA_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
#   Set in wa-ventera's outbound session webhook config.
# WA_OUTBOUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-outbound-secret-here

# ESCALATION_WA_NUMBER: phone number (e164 digits, e.g. 6281234567890) to notify
#   when Claude escalates a lead conversation to a human.
# ESCALATION_WA_NUMBER=6281234567890
